'''Victor Moritz''' "'''Mo''" '''Wagner''' (born 26 April 1997) is a German professional [[basketball]] player for the [[Orlando Magic]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA).<ref>{{cite web | title=It's Moe Wagner, Not Mo Wagner | first=Giri | last=Nathan | url=https://defector.com/its-moe-wagner-not-mo-wagner | date=December 4, 2024 | website=Defector | publisher=Defector Media LLC | location=New York | access-date=December 4, 2024}}</ref> He played for [[Alba Berlin]]<ref name=":0" /> before moving to the US to play college basketball for the [[Michigan Wolverines men's basketball|Michigan Wolverines]] from 2015 through his junior season for the [[2017–18 Michigan Wolverines men's basketball team|2017–18 Wolverines team]]. Wagner entered his name for the [[2017 NBA draft]] without hiring an agent, but withdrew and returned to Michigan. He was selected with the 25th overall pick in the [[2018 NBA draft]] by the [[Los Angeles Lakers]].

He was a 2018 All-Big Ten second team selection by both the coaches and the media. Following the season, he was the [[2018 Big Ten Conference men's basketball tournament]] MVP helping the team earn the Big Ten tournament championship for the second time in a row. He was also named to the West Region All-Tournament Team and Final Four All-Tournament Team during the [[2018 NCAA Division I men's basketball tournament|2018 NCAA basketball tournament]]. He has represented the [[Germany men's national basketball team|Germany national team]]. His younger brother [[Franz Wagner]] is also an NBA player as well as his teammate, playing [[small forward]] for the [[Orlando Magic]].
